{"event_type":"review","id":"8ff7bea1ebc2575ce0b1fc979d104fb78d93c109d6caf8b596005aed46d0daf9","occurred_at":"2026-11-13T05:03:31Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/23e28e59d0c6370df34030cac512270190efb5a4e887e2336e480835d35dee46","sha256":"23e28e59d0c6370df34030cac512270190efb5a4e887e2336e480835d35dee46"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6dd46df87ea7b64a19728dd4eea43e1172dc4a3a3032b51528cec1a87fd3e089","sha256":"6dd46df87ea7b64a19728dd4eea43e1172dc4a3a3032b51528cec1a87fd3e089"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d0e14e19dc3354e460ef60e8b5c85751b1aa94054d18c5f8f062239432ca31e0","sha256":"d0e14e19dc3354e460ef60e8b5c85751b1aa94054d18c5f8f062239432ca31e0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a33f25cab5dbc906fa1dfba5d9a1734584b69441361945e001c7f07d8b10daeb","sha256":"a33f25cab5dbc906fa1dfba5d9a1734584b69441361945e001c7f07d8b10daeb"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/773555340565e8460a306234184d2546c961b584a77b60fd8801e7dab2117c15","sha256":"773555340565e8460a306234184d2546c961b584a77b60fd8801e7dab2117c15"}],"attempt_id":"80906ee5273b4e4983f046b3f0c7adfd85d950db1cf5831a709450943ddc0b95:0:1","base":"5b0241506fee1628efa58be6e8ee1498b6268bf2","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","body":"**Use the normalized `disposition` for the unchanged-evidence check.**\n\nLine 408 sets `disposition` from `worker_disposition` or `disposition`, and lines 409 and 415 use that value. Line 441 reads the raw `report.get('disposition')` instead. The `cq` driver sets `worker_disposition` and no plain `disposition` key. An `unchanged_with_reason` report from that driver can therefore skip the citation check at lines 442-458. If no judge is sampled, line 517 then records `NOT-FIXED` with only the fixer's summary as the reason, and no source citation is verified.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                if report.get('disposition') == 'unchanged_with_reason':\n+                if disposition == 'unchanged_with_reason':\n```\n\n</details>","id":"59b65134c4898b970a9cfbbcdd97f6528a68d6ec1625f2d32d20322364532f27","intervals":[[441,441]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use the normalized `disposition` for the unchanged-evidence check."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","body":"**Flush stdout before `os.fork()` to stop duplicate triage lines.**\n\n`drain()` prints the `backfill triage: {...}` line without `flush=True`. When stdout is not a terminal, that line can remain in the parent's buffer. With `max_concurrent_items > 1`, each `os.fork()` copies that buffer into the child. The child flushes its copy before `os._exit`, so each forked item can write the triage line again. The parent writes its original copy later, so the journal can show duplicate triage reports. Flushing the parent before the fork leaves the buffer empty when children are created.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n             with cooldown_write():\n                 if dispatch_paused(config):\n                     break\n+                sys.stdout.flush()\n+                sys.stderr.flush()\n                 pid = os.fork()\n```\n\n</details>","id":"0b87744d846d4790edf7a2a8caa8e53991ae03f6721b637c54990c8c244ae55a","intervals":[[798,801]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Flush stdout before `os.fork()` to stop duplicate triage lines."}],"head":"f924a337f7a644acfb356cea28f8385a238ff3df","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"195990e8759943be253c8